  <bioghist id="aspace_51e8cdccfbd3ba3bcfc1d3a55fdbe9b5">
    <head>Biographical Note</head>
<p>Doug Ashford was born in Rabat, Morrocco in 1958. He graduated from the Cooper Union for the Advancement of Science and Art with a BFA in 1981. He is most known for being a member of the artists collective Group Material and was active participant in the Group from 1982 to its disbanding in 1996. He has worked on a number of public art projects including the "Who Cares" series with Creative Time in 2005. Since 1989, he has taught as a professor at Cooper Union and was tenured as a full professor in 2020.</p>  </bioghist>
  <prefercite id="aspace_f35c0607d4b54d4983fdf02a7fefcfa4">
